0 -1 7105 0
E
logbook~
You flip through the logbook and read of visits to faraway place
a couple of which you have even heard of. The Captain seemed to go
from place to place.. doing mostly trading, and some fishing if
there was something particularly interesting to catch. Whomever the
Captain hired as the Navigator, he also listed cargos and
crewmembers, This was probably the only book on the whole ship.
Toward the end of the book you read:
Capt'n was below decks today and was looking for Giblets his parrot
while the crew was hoisting cargo out of the hold when the line
slipped and the Capt'n took a nasty blow to the head. A full load
o' sacks of grain knocked him down, when he was uncovered. he ordered
"All 9 yards to the north shore!" which is silly since we only ever
had the 3 sails. Anyway. It's evening now and we abandoned the
grain delivery and are headed north with all speed.
~
E
compass~
It appears to still work.
~
S
#7107
Inside The Chicken Shack~
Being this close to the kitchen you can really smell the delicious
chicken cooking. Theres a heavy door with only a small hole in which
orders are placed and chicken is served. I guess Capt'n Clucky isn't
taking any chances with people snooping around his kitchen. Someone
might steal his recipe! You try to catch a glimpse inside the
kitchen, but are jostled and bumped out of the way by the servers
placing orders and picking up plates of hot food.
